# Agon 08_sand_casualpirates layers 6+7: SelectTarget's Two-state arms.  Two needs the body in the
# generate animation with a valid target (the SetTargetVector arm, taken), then the target deleted
# (the cast arm's false side) and then no target at all (the "is there a target" false side) while
# mState is still Two; the cycle is repeated because Two lasts only while the body is Generating.
@f300 layer 6
@f340 layer 7
@f560 god 1; give morphBall 1; give missile 20
@f580 send u0547 Activate; send u053d Activate; send u0539 Activate; send u0538 Activate; send u0535 Activate
@f600 objs pirate
@f620 place u04d8 355.43 -240.26 3.79; place u0547 355.43 -240.26 3.79
@f650 fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f900 obj u0547
@f950 send u04d8 Delete
@f1000 obj u0547; obj u04d8
@f1050 codecall u0547 SetPatrolDest
@f1080 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1110 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1140 obj u0547
@f1200 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f1400 send u0547 Alert
@f1500 codecall u0547 SetPatrolDest
@f1530 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1560 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1600 obj u0547; status
@f1700 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f1800 codecall u0547 SetPatrolDest
@f1830 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1860 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f1900 obj u0547
@f2000 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f2100 codecall u0547 SetPatrolDest
@f2130 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f2200 obj u0547; status
